// Constant arrays with an init list -- the cos/sin tables cpx_ball needs.
//
// A scalar #constant is FOLDED at the reference: `A = B` and `A = 5` compile to
// byte-identical code. An element chosen at RUN TIME cannot be folded, so an
// indexed reference has to emit a real load against the constant's own storage.
// If the fold were left in, every CT[..] here would come back as CT[0].

#constant CT[10] = { -100, -81, -31,  31,  81, 100,  81,  31, -31, -81 }
#constant ST[10] = {    0,  59,  95,  95,  59,   0, -59, -95, -95, -59 }

#variable I = 0
#variable a = 0
#variable b = 0
#variable c = 0
#variable d = 0

// Constant subscript: folds to the element's own declaration.
a = CT[0] ? 1
b = ST[3] ? 1

// Runtime subscript: one OP_SETOX per access. Reading two different elements
// through the same declaration is the whole point -- if the register cache in
// map_reg were allowed to serve an array, c and d would come out equal.
I = 6 ? 1
c = CT[I] ? 1
d = ST[I] ? 1
